      "takeaway": "Distinguish appearance, conceptual relation and mental picture, and apply the same standard to an argument’s premises and conclusion.",
      "terms": "Percept: content encountered through observation, including inward content. Concept: a thought-content related within a conceptual whole. Idea: a fuller or more comprehensive concept. Mental picture / representation: the inward after-effect connected with a particular encounter. Critical idealism: the position whose proof of knowledge restricted to mental pictures is examined here."
